Subject: [PATCH] base: a compiled-in nanfu kernel stamp

Adds base/nanfu/kernel_stamp.h, the one place a Nanfu build states which
upstream tag and which series revision it came from. Nothing includes it
yet: wiring it into a compiled target is a separate change that has to be
written on a checkout, because it edits existing BUILD.gn files. Until
then this patch is inert, and that is deliberate - it is the first entry
of the series, so it proves the series applies on a clean checkout at the
declared tag without touching a single line of upstream code.

The stamp is not exposed to page script anywhere in this series.

Nanfu-Patch-Applies-To: 155.0.8059.85
Nanfu-Patch-Promise: base/nanfu/kernel_stamp.h::nanfu-kernel-series:1;upstream=155.0.8059.85
Nanfu-Patch-Surfaces: none

diff --git a/base/nanfu/kernel_stamp.h b/base/nanfu/kernel_stamp.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bfcfaef9292587bfdede8b2dfa81a42d0ca28c68
--- /dev/null
+++ b/base/nanfu/kernel_stamp.h
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
